  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 22-layer planar multilayer filter on CaF2 substrate under air incidence. Stack sequence: ZnS, MgF2, ZnS, MgF2, ZnS, MgF2, ZnS, MgF2, ZnS, MgF2, ZnS, MgF2, ZnS, MgF2, ZnS, MgF2, ZnS, MgF2, ZnS, MgF2, ZnS, MgF2 (22 finite layers total). All layer thicknesses bounded to [700, 1100] nm. Optimize for high mean transmittance in 3250-3350 nm and 4200-4300 nm passbands, low mean transmittance in 2500-3100 nm and 4450-5000 nm stopbands. Include optical-path difference penalty in loss function to suppress thickness excursions and enforce smooth phase progression. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with coherent TMM solver. Normal unpolarized illumination. No metal layers. Evaluate all 22 thicknesses as continuous design variables. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 2500-3100 nm, 3250-3350 nm, 4200-4300 nm, 4450-5000 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 3.25-3.35 um and 4.20-4.30 um bands; Low transmittance in 2.50-3.10 um and 4.45-5.00 um bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: High transmittance in 2.50-3.10 um and 4.45-5.00 um bands. manufacturing constraints: Total layer count <= 24; No metal layers; Conventional depositable infrared inorganic dielectric materials only.",
